THE MOTIVES OF SCIENTISTS
-------------------------

<P>87. Science and technology provide the most important examples of
surrogate activities. [ interesting concept although i feel it conflicts
w/ the healthy innate human instinct to evolve] Some scientists claim that
they are motivated by "curiosity," that notion is simply absurd. Most
scientists work on highly specialized problem that are not the object of
any normal curiosity. For example, is an astronomer, a mathematician or an
